1.  **Input Sanitization:** Sanitize or encode all user-provided input (`msg`) to neutralize control characters (e.g., newlines, carriage returns, ANSI escape codes) before incorporating it into log entries. This prevents log injection attacks where an attacker could forge or manipulate log records.
